  "body": "Accept an explicit zero taper when a script or MCP client adds or edits a Wire Contour. The patch validator reads the typed operation value when the saved form omits its default. Other operation kinds and unknown fields retain their existing checks.\n\nThe regression test wire_contour_accepts_an_explicit_zero_taper_on_add_and_edit creates a vertical operation, sets a taper and clears it. It also checks a misspelled field and a field on the wrong operation kind.\n\nThe quick gate passed all 16 steps and 373 tests. Strict clippy passed on all camcraft-app targets. The normal CLI produced the same 331-byte vertical program for an omitted taper, zero, 0.0 and an edit from 3 degrees to zero. The 3 degree control produced 496 bytes. A misspelled field, a wire taper on a Face operation, and a string value each failed without an NC file. The release suite pocket3d_hsm failed on macOS (Apple silicon). The measured triple was 3158 moves, 3130 planar moves and 1141 arcs. Base commit 3ffe2338f reproduced these three counts and failed the same assertion. See #2371. The remaining heavy suites are running. Verification used the offline software only.\n\nEffort: high\nChangelog: A Wire Contour accepts an explicit zero taper on creation and when an edit returns it to a vertical cut.\n\nFixes #2925\n",
